 * version of GCC on the targets of two bugs of GCC 14, the version they
 * were found with.
 * Workaround: GCC 14, RISC-V: it crashes on a compare-and-exchange of 16
 * bits of a value it has just computed as a floating-point one, such as a
 * _Float16.
 * Workaround: GCC 14, MIPS with the o32 ABI: it passes a structure of 8
 * bytes aligned to 4, which was a parameter, to __atomic_exchange_8 of the
 * atomic library in the registers of such a structure, $5 and $6, rather
 * than in those of the integer that function takes, $6 and $7. */
