 * the builtins do not do: those on the integers of up to 4 bytes for the
 * targets of _FCXX_ATOMIC_MICROBLAZE, and those below.
 *
 * Workaround: GCC 16.1, MIPS: the builtins of the addition, the and, the or
 * and the exclusive or of the objects of 1 and 2 bytes compute their NAND
 * instead (16.2 computes them right), so those of the integers of 1 and 2
